    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know, i know... people always say that. but it doesn't feel like just \"feelings\" to me. it feels like biology. like there's this glitch in my code or something. i look in the mirror and i don't see me, i just see the end of the line. how am i supposed to fight something that's literally part of my cells?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very real and heavy feeling, that sense of being fundamentally broken by your own biology. Acknowledging that it feels like a biological script is a step, but it doesn't mean you have to play it out. Sometimes, the most effective way to fight a genetic predisposition is to find the one small thing that feels like a genuine break in the pattern. Consider reaching out to a psychiatrist who specializes in genetic predispositions; they can offer targeted ways to manage what feels like an inescapable code.",
